
====================================================================================================
S1. The dS-Unruh quadrature produces alpha = 1, exactly and rigidly
====================================================================================================
  T(a) = sqrt(H**2 + a**2)   (Deser-Levin quadrature)
  mu(a) = [T(a) - T(0)]/a = (-H + sqrt(H**2 + a**2))/a
    a >> H : 1   (Newtonian)
    a << H : a/(2*H)   (deep, linear in a)
  1 - mu in w = H/a : leading coefficient 1, i.e. 1 - mu ~ 1*(H/a)
  [OK] the quadrature's tail is LINEAR in H/a (coefficient 1), i.e. ALPHA = 1 -- the alpha=1 kernel is what the de Sitter-Unruh mechanism produces, not an arbitrary fit

  writing a = x a0 gives mu_q = (sqrt(x^2 + c^2) - c)/x with c = H/a0;
  matching mu_fw = (sqrt(x^2 + 1/4) - 1/2)/x forces c = 1/2, i.e. a0 = 2H = 2 c H_Lambda,
  which is MILGROM'S OWN COEFFICIENT -- an independent consistency check on the route.
  mu_q(c=1/2) = (sqrt(4*x**2 + 1) - 1)/(2*x) ;  mu_q - mu_fw = 0
  [OK] the quadrature at a0 = 2H is IDENTICALLY the framework's retired alpha=1 kernel -- so switching away from alpha=1 is switching away from the mechanism's own output, and the normalisation it forces is Milgrom's 2cH_Lambda, not the framework's cH_Lambda/Z

====================================================================================================
S2. No member of the quadrature family gives alpha = 2
====================================================================================================
  alpha = 2 requires mu = x/sqrt(1+x^2), i.e. a quadrature in 1/mu rather than in T.
  For T = f(sqrt(a^2+H^2)), the floor subtraction leaves a term linear in H/a whatever f is:
  f                               1-mu leading power of (H/a)   alpha
  sqrt(a^2+H^2)                                             1       1
  (a^2+H^2)^(1/4)                                          oo       1
  log(1+(a^2+H^2)/H^2)                                     oo       1
  [OK] all 3 quadrature variants give alpha = 1 -- the tail exponent is RIGID under this route, so alpha = 2 cannot be recovered from any of them

====================================================================================================
S3. Why the switch is still right: the derived kernel is excluded by data
====================================================================================================
  kernel                 source                      Earth anomaly  vs 2-sigma bound
  alpha=1 (retired)      dS-Unruh quadrature            4.6800e-11         1.28e+03x
  alpha=2 (adopted)      PHENOMENOLOGICAL               1.3167e-18         3.60e-05x
  So there is no option in which the framework keeps a DERIVED kernel: the derived one is
  excluded at 1279x. The choice is derived-and-excluded versus fitted-and-viable.
  [OK] the trade is stated as a trade, not as a free improvement

====================================================================================================
S4. The Cassini section of the de Sitter paper GETS STRONGER, and gains a missing item
====================================================================================================
  DESITTER_GAUGE_MOND_SCALE section 5.1 argues: at Saturn a/a0 = 6.9e5, so 1 - mu = 7.2e-7,
  a factor ~30 below the Cassini bound |gamma-1| < 2.3e-05. Recomputed:
  kernel                 1 - mu at Saturn   margin vs Cassini
  alpha=1 (retired)            7.2464e-07           3.17e+01x
  alpha=2 (adopted)            1.0503e-12           2.19e+07x
  [OK] the paper's own 7.2e-7 is reproduced (7.246e-07), validating the comparison before it is changed
  [OK] under alpha=2 the Saturn margin goes from 32x to 2.2e+07x -- the gamma test becomes vastly safer
  AND THE PAPER IS MISSING AN ITEM THAT alpha=2 ALSO FIXES. Section 5.1 tests only gamma-1.
  It never states the CONSTANT SUNWARD a0/2 anomaly, which under alpha=1 is 1279x over the
  Earth 2-sigma ephemeris bound -- a liability the paper does not mention and which the
  gamma argument does not cover. Under alpha=2 it drops to 3.6e-5x. So the update both
  strengthens a stated claim and closes an unstated gap.

====================================================================================================
S5. WHAT EACH OF THE THREE PAPERS MUST NOW SAY
====================================================================================================
  DESITTER_GAUGE_MOND_SCALE -- materially affected, because its whole thesis is the
    derived/posited split:
     * Eq. (4) becomes mu = x/sqrt(1+x^2); the clause 'g_obs = sqrt(g_N^2 + g_N a0)' and
       'the exact algebraic inverse of the de Sitter-Unruh quadrature' are WITHDRAWN.
     * item (ii) of the abstract must separate two things it currently fuses: the four
       certified mechanisms force the SCALING a0 ~ c^2 sqrt(Lambda); the dS-Unruh route
       additionally produced the KERNEL, and that part is now given up.
     * section 5.1 gains the ephemeris item and a far larger Cassini margin.
     * the kappa = 1/2 reduction, the SO(4,1) uniqueness and the FDR count are UNTOUCHED --
       none of them uses the tail.
  WB_CUBIC_GATE_LAW -- two numbers and a credit line:
     * the credit line's 'identity g_obs^2 - g_bar^2 = a0 g_bar' is an alpha=1 identity;
     * gamma_v ~ 1.09 becomes ~1.02 (Amendment 3 to the DR4 pre-registration), so the
       falsifier 'a boost gamma_v ~ 1.09 found inside 30 kAU' must be renumbered.
  CRISPY_DARK_MATTER -- credit line and reference only; no computed number in it depends on
    the tail, so the scientific content is unaffected.
  [OK] per-paper triage recorded before any paper is edited
